  (:adr/body "# Handing the drone work to the resident bots, and what the bots' own numbers say

Owner instruction (2026-08-30): \"ここまでの作業を itonami bots で引き継いで bots の
安定稼働を確認\".

## The handoff already happened, mechanically

The three libraries built this session (`kami-engine-rotor`, `-pack`,
`-multirotor`) are in `manifest/repo-bots.edn` and — the part that matters,
because the roster is not the running — they are in `~/.gftd/repo-bots/state.edn`,
**measured by the tick at 08:44 today.** The repo-bot fleet adopted them from
west without anyone asking it to, which is what the one-bot-per-repo design is
for. `celler` likewise.

That is `repo-bots` (per-repo floors: checkout / pinned / landed / readme /
test-signal). The `itonami bots` are a different fleet with a different job —
they raise cloud-itonami **maturity** and **coverage** — and the drone
libraries are kotoba-lang libraries, so they are not itonami-bot work. Saying
otherwise would hand the work to a fleet whose gate would correctly refuse it.

## Are the bots running stably? Measured, not assumed

Hermes scheduler: heartbeat 31 s old at the time of measurement, `ticker_last_success`
equal to it. Six itonami jobs registered and enabled.

| job | schedule | last run | status |
|---|---|---|---|
| itonami-ingest-scout | `5,35 * * * *` | 08:37 | ok |
| itonami-coverage-scout | `20,50 * * * *` | 08:41 | ok |
| mg-itonami-design | `15 3 * * *` | 04:21 | ok |
| itonami-capital-analysis | `25 6 * * *` | 07:31 | ok |
| itonami-research-collector | `10 16 * * *` | never | **first fire still ahead** |
| itonami-research-impact | `10 17 * * *` | never | **first fire still ahead** |

**Stable now; it was not yesterday.** Execution history over 48 h: the two
half-hourly scouts logged 31 completions and 19 failures, and the failures are
all in one window (2026-08-29 12:00 to 2026-08-30 00:00). Their errors name the
cause and it is not the bots:

```
RuntimeError: Non-streaming API call timed out after 90s   (x7)
RuntimeError: HTTP 502: murakumo fleet unreachable: Network connection lost
RuntimeError: HTTP 400: Loading model
RuntimeError: Context length exceeded (8,214 tokens)
Scheduler restarted before a durable terminal state         (x6, whether side effects ran is unknown)
```

**From 01:00 today: 20 consecutive completions, zero failures, eight hours.** The
incident was the murakumo inference fleet, and it cleared.

The two jobs with no runs were **created at 00:56 today** and their first
scheduled fire is 16:10 / 17:10. `Never ran` and `created an hour ago` are the
same shape in an execution table, and only one of them is a problem; these are
the second. They are UNVERIFIED, not broken, and this ADR does not claim they
work.

## One real finding in the bot fleet

`itonami-coverage-scout` committed at 08:41 today on
`bot/coverage-scout-20260830-0840` in `~/.gftd/worktrees/itonami-growth-bot`, and
**that commit is not on the remote** — GitHub has zero `bot/*` branches. The
bot's earlier output does land (main has ~197 lines of coverage register, many
added over the last two days), so this is not a dead pipeline; it is one
commit that stopped one step short.

Worse, it is half-redundant: the commit adds COFOG 033 (law courts) and
COFOG 105 (unemployment), and **105 is already on main**, carried there by
commit `516582f2570` whose message says it picked up \"sibling's uncommitted 105
entry\". Merging the branch as written would re-add a duplicate — the fleet has
already had a `fix: remove duplicate itonami coverage entries` commit once.

Deliberately NOT merged here. The 033 half is new and worth landing; the 105
half would recreate a known defect, and picking one half out of another agent's
commit is not a thing to do without saying so. It is recorded instead, which is
what ADR-2608273200 built the `ALREADY PUSHED, NOT MERGED` reporting for — except
this one is a step earlier and the collector cannot see it at all, because
GitHub cannot see it either. **The report says UNKNOWN for work that was never
pushed, and UNKNOWN is where this lived.**

## Resume point for the drone work

Landed and green: `kami-engine-rotor` (:rom-rotor), `kami-engine-pack`
(:rom-pack), `kami-engine-multirotor`, and `motor.bldc` (:rom-bldc) inside
`kami-engine-motor`. All four pinned in west; three `:jvm-test` fleet gates
registered.

Next, in order:

1. **Get one fleet gate green.** Three are registered and none has ever run on
   the fleet. By this workspace's own rule none of them is landed.
2. **A design actor.** The closure is a governor with nothing proposing to it.
   The shape to copy is `kami-engine-vehicle-designer` (DesignProposer sealed
   behind PhysicsGovernor).
3. **The UAS manufacturing and compliance vertical**, which IS itonami-bot
   territory: it is an ISIC 3030 question, and `cloud-itonami-isic-3030` contains
   zero occurrences of uav / drone / unmanned. `gftdcojp/defence` already holds
   the ITAR/ECCN classifier such a vertical would call.

Known inaccuracies that survive: no rotor-to-rotor interference, no ground
effect, no gust margin, no cooling, and a motor fit that averages over KV 100-400
with an 18.6% worst residual.

## Closing audit, 2026-08-30

Every repo touched this session is three-point aligned — local HEAD equals the
remote default branch equals the west pin, working tree clean:

| repo | commit |
|---|---|
| kotoba-lang/kami-engine-rotor | `fd8ea44` |
| kotoba-lang/kami-engine-pack | `ed2ff2d` |
| kotoba-lang/kami-engine-multirotor | `152cc59` |
| kotoba-lang/kami-engine-motor | `1dccf82` |
| kotoba-lang/celler | `35a42a7` |
| etzhayyim/root | `afb3e79` |

Superproject `com-junkawasaki/root` at `12c2a9a` and 0 ahead / 0 behind
`origin/main`. No open PRs in any of the seven repositories touched. No `agent/*`
branches of this session remain, local or remote. No worktrees of this session
remain.

**One stash retired.** `stash@{0}` — \"west.yml: kami-engine-pack entry (preserved
by ayatori-wiring session)\" — turned out to be this session's own work, stashed
by a concurrent session to get past it. Content-containment checked before
dropping: the stashed pack pin `0b28ee23` is an ancestor of main's `ed2ff2d`
(ahead=1, behind=0) and the stashed rotor pin `fd8ea447` is byte-identical to
main's. Archived to `.git/stash-archive-20260830/` first regardless, per the
retirement rule that confidence is not a reason to skip the archive.

Untouched on purpose: `90-docs/observatory/observatory.datoms.edn` (another
session's uncommitted work) and the worktree
`scratchpad/root-closing [agent/adr-write-path-ceiling]`, which belongs to a
different session.

### What was verified, and what was not

| | |
|---|---|
| ran green | kami-engine-rotor 20 tests / 69 assertions; kami-engine-pack 13 / 57; kami-engine-multirotor 14 / 65; kami-engine-motor 17 / 56 (bldc + the pre-existing solver suite). Both the `:dev` local-sibling path and the plain `:test` git-dep path the fleet gate takes. clj-kondo 0 errors 0 warnings on all four |
| verified discriminating | twelve deliberate breaks across the four repos, each reddening the tests that name it, each restored to green |
| **NOT run** | **every fleet gate.** Three `:jvm-test` gates are registered and none has executed on the fleet. By this workspace's own rule none of them is landed |
| **NOT run** | celler's TypeScript suite — `npm install` timed out at 180 s (exit 124) fetching the `@etzhayyim/sdk` git dependencies. The identity rewrite is textual-consistency checked only |
| not measured | whether the calibrated motor fit holds below 216 W or above 3180 W; the solver reports `:extrapolated?` there rather than guessing |

### First command for whoever picks this up

```
nbb scripts/fleet-ci/tick.cljs        # get one of the three gates to run
```

Until one is green, the correct summary of this session's test evidence is
\"green on this workstation\", not \"green\".")))